{"slug":"/students/subjects/chemistry/electrochemistry-redox/galvanic-cells/","source":"students/subjects/chemistry/electrochemistry-redox/galvanic-cells.html","area":"students","kind":"topic","title":"Galvanic Cells | Chemistry","description":"","subject":"chemistry","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <!-- Navigation -->\n    <nav class=\"mb-4 flex items-center justify-between\">\n      <a href=\"/students/subjects/chemistry/electrochemistry-redox/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 transition flex items-center\">\n        <span class=\"mi -arrow-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>Back to Electrochemistry &amp; Redox\n      </a>\n      <!-- Progress indicator -->\n      <div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\">\n        <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">\n          <span id=\"topic-progress-text\" data-bidemy=\"progress-text\">0% Complete</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"w-24 h-2 bg-gray-200 rounded-full overflow-hidden\" data-bidemy=\"progress\">\n          <div id=\"topic-progress-bar\" class=\"h-full bg-gradient-to-r from-green-400 to-emerald-500 transition-all duration-300\" style=\"width: 0%\"></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </nav>\n    \n    <article class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 shadow-lg\">\n      <!-- Header -->\n      <div class=\"border-b pb-4 mb-6\">\n        <h1 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2\">\n          <span class=\"mi -battery-full text-green-500 mr-3\" data-mi=\"battery_full\">battery_full</span>Galvanic (Voltaic) Cells\n        </h1>\n        <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Understanding electrochemical cells that convert chemical energy into electrical energy spontaneously.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n      <div class=\"bg-green-50 border-l-4 border-green-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-green-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n          <li>• Explain how a galvanic cell produces electricity</li>\n          <li>• Identify the anode and cathode in a galvanic cell</li>\n          <li>• Write cell notation using standard conventions</li>\n          <li>• Calculate cell potential from standard electrode potentials</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Section 1: What is a Galvanic Cell? -->\n      <section id=\"section-1\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n          What is a Galvanic Cell?\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-3\">A <strong class=\"text-green-600\">Galvanic (Voltaic) cell</strong> is an electrochemical cell that converts chemical energy from spontaneous redox reactions into electrical energy. Unlike electrolysis, galvanic cells generate electricity naturally!</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mt-3\">\n            <p class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Key Characteristics:</p>\n            <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n              <li>• Uses a <strong>spontaneous</strong> redox reaction</li>\n              <li>• Converts chemical energy → electrical energy</li>\n              <li>• Produces a positive cell potential (E°<sub>cell</sub> &gt; 0)</li>\n              <li>• Electrons flow from anode to cathode through external circuit</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Comparison with Electrolytic Cell -->\n        <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-green-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -battery-three-quarters mr-2\" data-mi=\"battery_std\">battery_std</span>Galvanic Cell</h4>\n            <ul class=\"text-green-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n              <li>• Spontaneous reaction</li>\n              <li>• Produces electricity</li>\n              <li>• No external power needed</li>\n              <li>• E°<sub>cell</sub> is positive</li>\n              <li>• Chemical → Electrical energy</li>\n              <li><strong>Examples:</strong> Batteries, fuel cells</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"bg-red-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-red-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-red-700 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -plug mr-2\" data-mi=\"power\">power</span>Electrolytic Cell</h4>\n            <ul class=\"text-red-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n              <li>• Non-spontaneous reaction</li>\n              <li>• Uses electricity</li>\n              <li>• External power required</li>\n              <li>• Applied voltage overcomes E°<sub>cell</sub></li>\n              <li>• Electrical → Chemical energy</li>\n              <li><strong>Examples:</strong> Electroplating, electrolysis</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 2: Parts of a Galvanic Cell -->\n      <section id=\"section-2\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n          Parts of a Galvanic Cell\n        </h2>\n\n        <!-- Diagram -->\n        <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"text-center\">\n            <svg viewBox=\"0 0 500 280\" class=\"w-full max-w-lg mx-auto\">\n              <!-- Left beaker (Anode) -->\n              <path d=\"M 50 100 L 50 220 Q 50 240 70 240 L 130 240 Q 150 240 150 220 L 150 100\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a5568\" stroke-width=\"2\"></path>\n              <rect x=\"50\" y=\"100\" width=\"100\" height=\"120\" fill=\"#fef3c7\" opacity=\"0.5\"></rect>\n              <text x=\"100\" y=\"260\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#4a5568\" font-size=\"11\">ZnSO</text></svg><sub>4</sub>(aq)\n              \n              <!-- Right beaker (Cathode) -->\n              <path d=\"M 350 100 L 350 220 Q 350 240 370 240 L 430 240 Q 450 240 450 220 L 450 100\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a5568\" stroke-width=\"2\">\n              <rect x=\"350\" y=\"100\" width=\"100\" height=\"120\" fill=\"#dbeafe\" opacity=\"0.5\">\n              <text x=\"400\" y=\"260\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#4a5568\" font-size=\"11\">CuSO<sub>4</sub>(aq)</text>\n              \n              <!-- Zinc electrode -->\n              <rect x=\"90\" y=\"60\" width=\"20\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#a0aec0\" rx=\"2\">\n              <text x=\"100\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#718096\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\">Zn</text>\n              \n              <!-- Copper electrode -->\n              <rect x=\"390\" y=\"60\" width=\"20\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#ed8936\" rx=\"2\">\n              <text x=\"400\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c05621\" font-size=\"10\" font-weight=\"bold\">Cu</text>\n              \n              <!-- Wire and voltmeter -->\n              <line x1=\"100\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"30\" stroke=\"#718096\" stroke-width=\"2\">\n              <line x1=\"100\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"30\" stroke=\"#718096\" stroke-width=\"2\">\n              <rect x=\"200\" y=\"15\" width=\"100\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#4a5568\" rx=\"3\">\n              <text x=\"250\" y=\"35\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"white\" font-size=\"10\">V</text>\n              <line x1=\"300\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"30\" stroke=\"#718096\" stroke-width=\"2\">\n              <line x1=\"400\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#718096\" stroke-width=\"2\">\n              \n              <!-- Salt bridge -->\n              <path d=\"M 170 140 Q 250 120 330 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#48bb78\" stroke-width=\"6\">\n              <path d=\"M 170 145 L 170 180\" stroke=\"#48bb78\" stroke-width=\"6\">\n              <path d=\"M 330 145 L 330 180\" stroke=\"#48bb78\" stroke-width=\"6\">\n              <text x=\"250\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#276749\" font-size=\"10\">Salt Bridge</text>\n              \n              <!-- Labels -->\n              <text x=\"100\" y=\"175\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#e53e3e\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"bold\">ANODE</text>\n              <text x=\"100\" y=\"188\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#e53e3e\" font-size=\"8\">(-)</text>\n              <text x=\"400\" y=\"175\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3182ce\" font-size=\"9\" font-weight=\"bold\">CATHODE</text>\n              <text x=\"400\" y=\"188\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3182ce\" font-size=\"8\">(+)</text>\n              \n              <!-- Electron flow -->\n              <text x=\"250\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#e53e3e\" font-size=\"9\">e⁻ flow →</text>\n              \n              <!-- Ion labels -->\n              <text x=\"100\" y=\"140\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#b7791f\" font-size=\"8\">Zn²⁺</text>\n              <text x=\"400\" y=\"140\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#3182ce\" font-size=\"8\">Cu²⁺</text>\n            \n          </path></path></path></line></line></rect></line></line></rect></rect></rect></path></div>\n          <p class=\"text-center text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2\">Daniel Cell: A common type of galvanic cell</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n          <div class=\"bg-red-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-red-500\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-red-800 flex items-center\">\n              <span class=\"mi -minus-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>Anode (Negative Electrode)\n            </h4>\n            <ul class=\"text-red-700 text-sm mt-2 space-y-1\">\n              <li>• Where <strong>oxidation</strong> occurs</li>\n              <li>• Electrons flow OUT from anode</li>\n              <li>• Metal electrode dissolves (loses mass)</li>\n              <li>• In Daniel Cell: Zn → Zn²⁺ + 2e⁻</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 flex items-center\">\n              <span class=\"mi -plus-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"add_circle\">add_circle</span>Cathode (Positive Electrode)\n            </h4>\n            <ul class=\"text-blue-700 text-sm mt-2 space-y-1\">\n              <li>• Where <strong>reduction</strong> occurs</li>\n              <li>• Electrons flow INTO cathode</li>\n              <li>• Metal deposits on electrode (gains mass)</li>\n              <li>• In Daniel Cell: Cu²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Cu</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-4 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800 flex items-center\">\n              <span class=\"mi -bridge mr-2\" data-mi=\"help_outline\">help_outline</span>Salt Bridge\n            </h4>\n            <ul class=\"text-green-700 text-sm mt-2 space-y-1\">\n              <li>• Contains inert electrolyte (e.g., KNO₃, KCl)</li>\n              <li>• Completes the circuit by allowing ion flow</li>\n              <li>• Maintains electrical neutrality in each half-cell</li>\n              <li>• Anions flow to anode; Cations flow to cathode</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 3: Cell Notation -->\n      <section id=\"section-3\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n          Cell Notation (Shorthand)\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-3\">Cell notation is a shorthand way to represent a galvanic cell without drawing a diagram.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">General Format:</p>\n            <div class=\"bg-gray-100 p-3 rounded text-center font-mono text-lg mb-3\">\n              Anode | Anode ion || Cathode ion | Cathode\n            </div>\n            <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n              <li>• <strong>|</strong> = Phase boundary (between solid and solution)</li>\n              <li>• <strong>||</strong> = Salt bridge (separates two half-cells)</li>\n              <li>• Anode (oxidation) written on the left</li>\n              <li>• Cathode (reduction) written on the right</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Example -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden mb-4\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-green-50 text-left font-semibold text-green-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-green-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2 text-yellow-500\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Example: Daniel Cell Notation</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded-lg text-center font-mono text-lg mb-3\">\n                Zn(s) | Zn²⁺(aq) || Cu²⁺(aq) | Cu(s)\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"space-y-2 text-sm\">\n                <p><strong>Zn(s) | Zn²⁺(aq)</strong> → Anode half-cell (oxidation: Zn → Zn²⁺ + 2e⁻)</p>\n                <p><strong>||</strong> → Salt bridge</p>\n                <p><strong>Cu²⁺(aq) | Cu(s)</strong> → Cathode half-cell (reduction: Cu²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Cu)</p>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 4: Cell Potential -->\n      <section id=\"section-4\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n          Calculating Cell Potential\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-3\">The cell potential (voltage) tells us the \"driving force\" of the reaction. It's calculated using standard electrode potentials (E° values).</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mb-3\">\n            <p class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Formula:</p>\n            <div class=\"bg-green-100 p-3 rounded text-center font-mono text-lg\">\n              E°<sub>cell</sub> = E°<sub>cathode</sub> - E°<sub>anode</sub>\n            </div>\n            <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2 text-center\">Or: E°<sub>cell</sub> = E°<sub>reduction</sub> - E°<sub>oxidation</sub></p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -info-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"info\">info</span>Important Points</h4>\n            <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n              <li>• For a spontaneous cell, E°<sub>cell</sub> must be <strong>positive</strong></li>\n              <li>• Standard electrode potentials are measured at 25°C, 1 M, 1 atm</li>\n              <li>• More positive E° = stronger oxidizing agent (better at gaining e⁻)</li>\n              <li>• More negative E° = stronger reducing agent (better at losing e⁻)</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Worked Example -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-purple-50 text-left font-semibold text-purple-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-purple-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -calculator mr-2 text-purple-500\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span>Worked Example: Calculate E° for Daniel Cell</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Given: E°(Zn²⁺/Zn) = -0.76 V and E°(Cu²⁺/Cu) = +0.34 V</p>\n              \n              <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Identify cathode and anode</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-purple-700 mt-1\">Cu has more positive E°, so Cu²⁺ is reduced (cathode)<br>Zn is oxidized (anode)</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-green-500\">\n                  <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Apply the formula</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 font-mono mt-1\">E°<sub>cell</sub> = E°<sub>cathode</sub> - E°<sub>anode</sub></p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 font-mono mt-1\">E°<sub>cell</sub> = (+0.34 V) - (-0.76 V)</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-green-700 font-mono mt-1\">E°<sub>cell</sub> = +1.10 V</p>\n                </div>\n                \n                <div class=\"bg-green-100 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                  <p class=\"text-green-800 font-semibold\"><span class=\"mi -check-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"check_circle\">check_circle</span>Answer: E°<sub>cell</sub> = +1.10 V (spontaneous)</p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 5: Video -->\n      <section id=\"section-5\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-green-100 text-green-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">5</span>\n          Video: Galvanic Cells Explained\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n          <div class=\"video-container\">\n            <iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/7b34XYgADlM\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen=\"\"></iframe>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 6: Practice Problems -->\n      <section id=\"section-6\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-green-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>\n          Practice Problems\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. In a galvanic cell, electrons flow from the _____ to the _____ through the external circuit.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <strong>Anode to Cathode</strong> - The anode is where oxidation occurs (loses electrons), and electrons flow to the cathode where reduction occurs (gains electrons).\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. Write the cell notation for a cell with Mg(s)|Mg²⁺(aq) as the anode and Ag⁺(aq)|Ag(s) as the cathode.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <strong>Mg(s) | Mg²⁺(aq) || Ag⁺(aq) | Ag(s)</strong>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. Calculate E°<sub>cell</sub> if E°(Mg²⁺/Mg) = -2.37 V and E°(Ag⁺/Ag) = +0.80 V.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>E°<sub>cell</sub> = E°<sub>cathode</sub> - E°<sub>anode</sub></p>\n                <p>E°<sub>cell</sub> = (+0.80 V) - (-2.37 V)</p>\n                <p>E°<sub>cell</sub> = <strong>+3.17 V</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 7: Key Takeaways -->\n      <section id=\"section-7\" class=\"mb-8\">\n      <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-green-50 to-emerald-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-green-200\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-green-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n          <li>• Galvanic cells convert chemical energy to electrical energy spontaneously</li>\n          <li>• Anode = oxidation (negative); Cathode = reduction (positive)</li>\n          <li>• Electrons flow: Anode → external circuit → Cathode</li>\n          <li>• Cell notation: Anode | Anode ion || Cathode ion | Cathode</li>\n          <li>• E°<sub>cell</sub> = E°<sub>cathode</sub> - E°<sub>anode</sub> (must be positive for spontaneous reaction)</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Complete Topic Button -->\n      <div class=\"mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200\">\n        <div class=\"flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4\">\n          <div class=\"text-center sm:text-left\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800\">Ready to Complete?</h3>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">View all sections, then take the quiz to mark this topic as complete.</p>\n          </div>\n          <button id=\"topic-complete-btn\" disabled=\"\" class=\"px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-gray-300 text-gray-500 cursor-not-allowed opacity-50 flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-medium\">\n            <span class=\"mi -lock mr-2\" data-mi=\"lock\">lock</span>\n            <span>Complete (0% viewed)</span>\n          </button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n\n  \n\n  <!-- Topic Tracking and Quiz System -->\n  \n\n\n<div data-bidemy=\"quiz\"></div>","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-green-50 to-emerald-100 p-4 md:p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body{font-family:Inter, sans-serif}\n    .content-card{-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(12px);backdrop-filter:blur(12px);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.95);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);} \n    .accordion-content{max-height:0;overflow:hidden;transition:max-height 0.3s ease-out;}\n    .accordion-content.open{max-height:2000px;}\n    .step-card{transition:all 0.2s ease;}\n    .step-card:hover{transform:translateX(4px);}\n    .video-container{position:relative;width:100%;padding-bottom:56.25%;height:0;overflow:hidden;border-radius:8px;background:#f9fafb;}\n    .video-container iframe{position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;border:none;}"],"quiz":{"topicId":"galvanic-cells","subject":"chemistry","passingScore":60,"questions":[{"question":"In a galvanic cell, where does oxidation occur?","options":["At the cathode","At the anode","In the salt bridge","In the external circuit"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Oxidation always occurs at the anode. Remember: Anode is where electrons are lost (oxidation)."},{"question":"What is the purpose of a salt bridge in a galvanic cell?","options":["To generate electricity","To complete the circuit by allowing ion flow","To increase the voltage","To store the electrodes"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The salt bridge completes the circuit by allowing ions to flow between half-cells, maintaining electrical neutrality."},{"question":"In the Daniel Cell, what happens at the zinc electrode?","options":["Cu²⁺ is reduced to Cu","Zn²⁺ is reduced to Zn","Zn is oxidized to Zn²⁺","Cu is oxidized to Cu²⁺"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Zinc is the anode where oxidation occurs: Zn → Zn²⁺ + 2e⁻"},{"question":"What does E°cell = +1.10 V indicate?","options":["The reaction is non-spontaneous","The reaction is spontaneous","The cell needs external power","No reaction occurs"],"correct":1,"explanation":"A positive E°cell indicates a spontaneous reaction. The cell can generate electricity without external power."},{"question":"Write the cell notation for Zn|Zn²⁺||Cu²⁺|Cu. What is the cathode?","options":["Zn","Zn²⁺","Cu","Cu²⁺"],"correct":2,"explanation":"In cell notation, the right side is the cathode. Cu²⁺|Cu means Cu is the cathode where reduction occurs."},{"question":"If E°(Zn²⁺/Zn) = -0.76 V and E°(Cu²⁺/Cu) = +0.34 V, calculate E°cell","options":["-1.10 V","+0.42 V","+1.10 V","-0.42 V"],"correct":2,"explanation":"E°cell = E°cathode - E°anode = (+0.34) - (-0.76) = +1.10 V"},{"question":"Which way do electrons flow in a galvanic cell?","options":["Cathode to anode through the external circuit","Anode to cathode through the external circuit","Anode to cathode through the salt bridge","Cathode to anode through the solution"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Electrons flow from the anode (where they are produced) to the cathode (where they are consumed) through the external circuit."},{"question":"Which electrode is negative in a galvanic cell?","options":["Cathode","Anode","Both electrodes","Neither electrode"],"correct":1,"explanation":"The anode is negative because it is the source of electrons. Oxidation releases electrons, making it electron-rich (negative)."}]},"tracker":{"topicId":"galvanic-cells","topicTitle":"Galvanic (Voltaic) Cells","subject":"chemistry","sections":["section-1","section-2","section-3","section-4","section-5","section-6","section-7"],"quizRequired":true},"links":[]}